                    <div class="eq-question">Which component is the ONLY one that reads/writes etcd?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>The <strong>kube-apiserver</strong>. Every other component (scheduler, controller-manager, kubelet) reaches state <em>through</em> the apiserver, never etcd directly.</p>
                        <div class="diagram-container">
                            <div class="diagram-title">the star topology — one gateway to state</div>
<pre>
  📋 scheduler ─┐                      ┌─ 🤖 kubelets
  🔄 ctrl-mgr ──┼──▶ 📡 apiserver ◀───┼─ ⌨️ kubectl
  controllers ──┘         │           └─ 🌐 kube-proxy
                          ▼  the ONLY client
                       🗄️ etcd  (all state)
</pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>This star topology is why an etcd backup = a cluster backup, and why securing/operating the apiserver is so critical.</p></div>
