                                <p><strong>Note:</strong> <code>kubectl get componentstatuses</code> (or <code>cs</code>) is <strong>deprecated</strong> since v1.19, but may still appear on the CKA. It checks health endpoints of control plane components. If the scheduler is unhealthy: (1) The scheduler static pod may have crashed — check its manifest in <code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/</code>, (2) The scheduler's health endpoint may be unreachable. Symptoms of a dead scheduler: new pods stay in <code>Pending</code> state because nothing assigns them to nodes. Existing pods continue running — only new scheduling decisions are blocked.</p>
