            <div class="cka-practice-drill">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 4.4 — Namespaces: Isolation, Scope &amp; Cross-NS DNS</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 7 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>Build the two-environment layout: namespaces <code>easypj-dev</code> and <code>easypj-prod</code>, one deployment in each. Then answer with commands, not opinions: (1) can two deployments share one name? (2) which resources ignore namespaces entirely? (3) how does a dev pod reach the prod Service by DNS?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> Names must be unique <em>per namespace</em>, not per cluster. <code>kubectl api-resources --namespaced=false</code> lists the cluster-wide escapees. Cross-namespace DNS is the FQDN: <code>svc.namespace.svc.cluster.local</code>.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                            <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">two environments, one cluster</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># 1. Two namespaces, same-named deployment in each — no conflict</span>
kubectl create ns easypj-dev
kubectl create ns easypj-prod
kubectl create deployment easypj-web --image=easypj:v1 -n easypj-dev
kubectl create deployment easypj-web --image=easypj:v2 --replicas=3 -n easypj-prod
kubectl get deploy -A | grep easypj-web    <span class="comment"># both exist — names are per-namespace ✅</span>

<span class="comment"># 2. What ignores namespaces? the cluster-scoped resources</span>
kubectl api-resources --namespaced=false | head
<span class="comment">#   nodes · persistentvolumes · storageclasses · namespaces · clusterroles …</span>

<span class="comment"># 3. Cross-namespace DNS — short name inside, FQDN across</span>
kubectl expose deploy easypj-web --port=80 --target-port=8000 -n easypj-prod
kubectl run tmp -n easypj-dev --image=busybox:1.28 --rm -it --restart=Never -- \
  nslookup easypj-web.easypj-prod.svc.cluster.local   <span class="comment"># resolves ✅</span>
<span class="comment">#   (plain "easypj-web" from easypj-dev would NOT resolve — wrong namespace)</span>

<span class="comment"># 4. Set your working namespace once instead of typing -n forever</span>
