                <div class="info-box note">
                    <h5>📖 What "Integrates With" Actually Means Here</h5>
                    <p>When this guide says Backstage "integrates with GitHub, Jenkins, Kubernetes, PagerDuty, Sentry, Jira, and Slack," it means: a <strong>Plugin</strong> for that tool calls that tool's own API and renders the result as a card on an entity page. Nothing about GitHub, Jenkins, or Kubernetes changes — Backstage is a <em>read (and sometimes write) client</em> sitting in front of tools that keep doing their own job.</p>
                </div>

                <h4>Just as Important — What Backstage Deliberately Does NOT Do</h4>
                <p>Knowing the hub's boundaries is as useful as knowing its job. Backstage never becomes any of the tools it surfaces:</p>
