            <section class="section-block" id="b-s1-9">
                <h3 class="section-h">1.9 Terminology Starter Pack — Your First 12 Words</h3>
                <p>Backstage has its own vocabulary, and it's used precisely — "Entity," "Kind," "Component," and "Resource" all mean specific, different things. Learn these 12 words now and every later chapter reads noticeably easier. (The full A–Z glossary lives in Appendix F — this is just the starter kit.)</p>

                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Plain-English meaning</th><th>You'll meet it again in…</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><code>Entity</code></td><td>Any "thing" Backstage tracks — a service, a database, a team, a person…</td><td>Ch 3, 7</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Kind</code></td><td>The <em>type</em> of entity (<code>Component</code>, <code>API</code>, <code>Resource</code>, <code>System</code>…)</td><td>Ch 3, 8</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Catalog</code></td><td>The searchable list of ALL entities</td><td>Ch 7</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Component</code></td><td>An entity for software <em>you</em> build (like jobpost)</td><td>Ch 3, 8</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Resource</code></td><td>An entity for infrastructure you <em>use</em> (like a Postgres database)</td><td>Ch 3, 8</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Plugin</code></td><td>An installable feature or extension</td><td>Ch 16-18</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Template</code></td><td>A blueprint for scaffolding new projects</td><td>Ch 11-13</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Scaffolder</code></td><td>The engine that <em>runs</em> Templates</td><td>Ch 11</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>TechDocs</code></td><td>Docs-as-code, published from Markdown</td><td>Ch 14-15</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Annotation</code></td><td>A key:value tag linking an entity to an external tool</td><td>Ch 3, 9</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Frontend</code></td><td>The React app you see in your browser</td><td>Ch 2</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>Backend</code></td><td>The Node.js server that does the real work</td><td>Ch 2</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box tip">
                    <h5>💡 One Sentence That Unlocks 80% of the Vocabulary</h5>
                    <p><strong>"An Entity is a THING, a Kind is its TYPE, and an Annotation is a STICKY NOTE that tells a Plugin where to find more info about it."</strong> Memorize that single sentence — it's the mental key to nearly every term above, and it's called out again in this chapter's Speed Tips because of how often it pays off.</p>
                </div>

                <h4>5 Bonus Words You'll See Very Soon</h4>
                <p>The 12 words above are the starter kit. These 5 show up the moment jobpost's full picture comes together (§1.12) — worth previewing now so they aren't a surprise:</p>
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Plain-English meaning</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><code>Namespace</code></td><td>A grouping boundary for entities — almost every org just uses <code>default</code> (Under the Hood §⑥)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>System</code></td><td>A grouping of related Components/APIs/Resources that work together (e.g. <code>easypj-system</code>)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>Domain</code></td><td>A grouping of related Systems, one level up (e.g. <code>hr-domain</code>)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>Group</code></td><td>A team or org unit that can own entities (e.g. <code>team-easypj</code>)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>Location</code></td><td>A pointer telling the Catalog WHERE to find an entity's <code>catalog-info.yaml</code></td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">The Vocabulary, Nested — From Broadest Grouping Down to One Entity</div>
<pre>
   🌐 Domain          hr-domain            ← broadest grouping (§1.9 bonus word)
       └── 📦 System       easypj-system        ← related pieces that work together
              ├── Component   jobpost              ← Kind: software you build
              ├── API         jobpost-api          ← Kind: a contract others can call
              └── Resource    jobpost-db           ← Kind: infrastructure you use
   👥 Group           team-easypj          ← owns any of the above (a team)
</pre>
