                    <div class="eq-question">Give the official, verbatim definition of Backstage — and explain why the word "framework" in it is doing real work.</div>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>"Backstage is an open source <strong>framework</strong> for building developer portals." It's a framework, not a finished portal — you assemble your org's own portal from Backstage's pieces (Catalog engine, Scaffolder, TechDocs pipeline, Plugin API), which is exactly why "Customizing Backstage" is 32% of the CBA exam, the biggest single domain.</p>
                        <div class="diagram-container">
                            <div class="diagram-title">"Framework" in one picture</div>
<pre>
  📦 Product (e.g. Gmail)          🧩 Framework (Backstage)
  install → done, ready to use     install → a SKELETON: Catalog engine,
                                    Scaffolder, TechDocs pipeline, Plugin API
