                <div class="info-box note">
                    <h5>📖 Key Term — Yarn Workspaces (and What <code>package.json</code> Even Is)</h5>
                    <p>Every folder above with its own <code>package.json</code> is a Node.js <strong>package</strong> — a small manifest file listing that package's name, its dependencies (other packages it needs), and the commands that can run it (like <code>start</code> or <code>build</code>). It's the Node.js equivalent of a Python project's <code>requirements.txt</code>, but richer.</p>
                    <p class="mb-0">A <strong>monorepo</strong> is one Git repository holding multiple independently-versioned packages. <strong>Yarn workspaces</strong> is the tool that makes this practical — a single <code>yarn install</code> at the repo root links <code>packages/app</code>, <code>packages/backend</code>, and every plugin together, so a change to a shared type is instantly visible everywhere without publishing to npm first.</p>
