                        <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p><strong>RBAC/permissions</strong> — "Forbidden" is a 403, meaning authentication already succeeded (the fresh token proves it). The fix is in the permission policy, not the token.</p>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>Evidence</th><th>Rules out</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>Token refreshed 2 min ago</td><td>401 (auth) — token is valid</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>"Forbidden" response</td><td>Confirms 403 (permissions)</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation">
                            <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                            <p>Under the Hood §②'s 3-check sequence: signature and expiry both passed (that's why it's not a 401); check 3 (permission policy) is what's failing.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
