                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Using SQLite in production.</strong> It only supports one writer — PostgreSQL is mandatory once you scale past one replica (§4.4).</li>
                    <li><strong>Assuming <code>yarn dev</code>'s clean startup means your types are correct.</strong> It transpiles without checking — run <code>yarn tsc</code> to actually verify (Under the Hood §①).</li>
                    <li><strong>Editing <code>app-config.yaml</code> and expecting it to hot-reload.</strong> Config changes need a restart (<code>Ctrl+C</code>, then <code>yarn dev</code> again); only theme/code changes hot-reload (§4.5).</li>
                    <li><strong>Assuming the frontend can call GitHub/Jenkins/etc. directly.</strong> It always goes through the backend proxy (§4.6).</li>
                    <li><strong>Following old guides that say "Node 18+" or "Yarn v1.22/v3+."</strong> Current official guidance is Node 22/24 and Yarn 4.4.1 via Corepack (§4.1).</li>
                </ul>
