                <h4>Detailed Walkthrough of Each Step</h4>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">📦</div>
                        <h5>Step 1: Create the Backstage App</h5>
                        <p><code>npx @backstage/create-app@latest</code> → Name it <strong>easypj-portal</strong>. Choose SQLite for dev. This creates ~147 files in a standard structure. Run <code>yarn dev</code> to verify the empty portal is running on <code>http://localhost:3000</code>.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🔑</div>
                        <h5>Step 2: Configure GitHub Integration</h5>
                        <p>Generate a <strong>GitHub Personal Access Token</strong> (Settings → Developer Settings → PAT). Add <code>integrations.github[0].token: ${GITHUB_TOKEN}</code> to <code>app-config.yaml</code>. Set <code>export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxx</code> before starting Backstage.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">📋</div>
                        <h5>Step 3: Define easypj Entities</h5>
                        <p>Create <code>catalog-info.yaml</code> in the jobpost repo. Define the <strong>Component</strong> (jobpost), <strong>API</strong> (jobpost-api), <strong>System</strong> (easypj), and <strong>Resources</strong> (postgres, redis). Add the catalog location URL to app-config.yaml.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">📝</div>
                        <h5>Step 4: Create a Django Software Template</h5>
                        <p>Create <code>template.yaml</code> defining parameters (service name, description, team). Create a <code>skeleton/</code> folder with boilerplate files: Dockerfile, requirements.txt, manage.py, catalog-info.yaml, k8s manifests. Register the template in app-config.yaml.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">📖</div>
                        <h5>Step 5: Set Up TechDocs</h5>
                        <p>Add <code>mkdocs.yml</code> and <code>/docs/</code> folder to the jobpost repo. Add <code>backstage.io/techdocs-ref: dir:.</code> annotation to catalog-info.yaml. TechDocs auto-builds docs from Markdown files when the entity page loads.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">✅</div>
                        <h5>Step 6: Verify Everything</h5>
                        <p>Visit <code>/catalog</code> → see all entities. Visit <code>/create</code> → see Django template. Click jobpost → see Docs tab with rendered TechDocs. Search for "jobpost" → entity appears. Run <code>curl :7007/api/catalog/entities</code> for API verification.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Step 3 in Detail: catalog-info.yaml for jobpost</div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml"># /jobpost/catalog-info.yaml — Entity definition
apiVersion: backstage.io/v1alpha1
kind: Component
metadata:
  name: jobpost
  description: Job posting and recruitment management service
  annotations:
    github.com/project-slug: easypj/jobpost
    backstage.io/techdocs-ref: dir:.
    backstage.io/kubernetes-namespace: easypj-prod
  tags:
    - django
    - python
    - recruitment
  links:
    - url: https://jobpost.easypj.com
      title: Production URL
      icon: dashboard
spec:
  type: service
  lifecycle: production
  owner: team-platform
  system: easypj-system
  dependsOn:
    - resource:postgres-db
    - resource:redis-cache
  providesApis:
    - jobpost-api</code></pre>
