            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch6-uth"></span>
            <details class="uth">
                <summary>Under the Hood — why setup mistakes fail silently, not loudly</summary>
                <div class="uth-body">
                    <p>§6.4's mistake table is really describing one underlying mechanism from Chapter 3 §3.3: the entity lifecycle only starts once ingestion successfully fetches a Location target.</p>
                    <h5>① Silent Ingestion Failure</h5>
                    <pre class="uth-diagram">
Location points at feature branch (not default)  →  ingestion never fetches it  →  NO error, entity just never appears
GitHub token lacks repo scope                     →  ingestion never fetches it  →  NO error, entity just never appears
                    </pre>
                    <div class="uth-callout mb-0"><strong>🔑 Backstage does not error loudly here</strong> — it simply never surfaces the entity, which is exactly why §6.3's checklist insists on actually LOOKING for jobpost in the Catalog rather than assuming a clean <code>yarn dev</code> startup means success.</div>
                </div>
            </details>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch6-takeaways"></span>
            <div class="key-takeaways">
                <h4>🔑 Key Takeaways</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Plan before you build:</strong> know your catalog seed, first template, and docs before running a command (§6.1).</li>
                    <li><strong>The 6-step build is:</strong> create app → GitHub integration → define entities → register Location → TechDocs → K8s plugin (§6.2).</li>
                    <li><strong>"It didn't crash" is not verification</strong> — use the §6.3 checklist and actually look for jobpost in the Catalog.</li>
                    <li><strong>SQLite-for-prod, token scope, and wrong-branch Locations</strong> are the top first-time mistakes (§6.4).</li>
                    <li><strong>A missing <code>docs/</code> folder or <code>mkdocs.yml</code></strong> is the #1 cause of a TechDocs 404 (§6.4).</li>
                    <li><strong>One working instance is a proof of concept, not a rollout</strong> — later parts cover scaling entities, templates, and teams (§6.5).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch6-gotchas"></span>
            <div class="cka-gotcha">
                <h5>⚠️ Common Gotchas &amp; Misconceptions</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Pointing a catalog Location at a feature branch</strong> instead of the default branch — the entity silently never appears (§6.4).</li>
                    <li><strong>Creating a GitHub token with no <code>repo</code> or <code>read:org</code> scopes</strong>, then blaming Backstage for a 404 (§6.4).</li>
                    <li><strong>Treating a template that "scaffolds" as done</strong> — if the token lacks repo-creation permission, the repo itself is never created (§6.4).</li>
                    <li><strong>Assuming <code>yarn dev</code> starting cleanly means the whole setup is correct</strong> (§6.3).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch6-speed"></span>
            <div class="cka-speed-tip">
                <h5>⚡ Speed Tips</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Always run through the §6.3 checklist top to bottom</strong> after any first-time setup, before declaring it "done."</li>
                    <li><strong>When TechDocs 404s, check <code>docs/</code>, then <code>mkdocs.yml</code>, then the <code>techdocs-ref</code> annotation</strong>, in that order (§6.4).</li>
                    <li><strong>Chapter 6 quick win:</strong> the Catalog is the first thing to set up — register entities via GitHub URLs or local files, verify with <code>curl http://localhost:7007/api/catalog/entities</code>. Templates are the second priority.</li>
                    <li><strong>Know the 5 key directories:</strong> <code>packages/app/src</code> (frontend), <code>packages/backend/src</code> (backend), <code>plugins/</code> (custom plugins), <code>app-config.yaml</code> (main config), <code>catalog-info.yaml</code> (entity definitions).</li>
