                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">What is the difference between a System and a Domain? When would you create each?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <pre class="uth-diagram">
hr-domain (Domain)
 ├── easypj-system (System) → jobpost, jobpost-api, postgres-db, redis-cache
 └── payroll-system (System) → payroll-api, payroll-db
                        </pre>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>System = technical grouping of Components/Resources. Domain = business grouping of multiple Systems. Create a System when 2+ Components work together; create a Domain when you have multiple Systems in the same business area.</p></div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">Write a complete Component YAML for the easypj jobpost service, including at least 3 annotations.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <div class="code-block-wrapper"><div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">catalog-info.yaml</span></div><pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: backstage.io/v1alpha1
kind: Component
metadata:
  name: jobpost
  description: Job posting and recruitment service
  annotations:
    github.com/project-slug: easypj/jobpost
    backstage.io/techdocs-ref: dir:.
    backstage.io/kubernetes-namespace: easypj-prod
  tags: [python, django, recruitment]
spec:
  type: service
  lifecycle: production
  owner: team-platform
  system: easypj-system
  providesApis: [jobpost-api]
