            <div class="chapter-intro">
            <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 9 · Catalog YAML &amp; Descriptors — Writing catalog-info.yaml</h2>
            <p class="chapter-lead">
                Every entity in Backstage is defined in a <strong>catalog-info.yaml</strong> file.
                <code>catalog-info.yaml</code> is the one file every easypj repo needs to join the Catalog. Get its
                structure wrong — a missing <code>apiVersion</code>, a typo'd <code>kind</code> — and jobpost
                silently fails to ingest, which is exactly the kind of problem Chapter 7 §7.7 taught you to debug.
                This chapter is what stops that problem happening in the first place.
            </p>
            <div class="chapter-meta">
                <span class="meta-tag">🟡 Intermediate</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">⏱️ ~2 hours</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">📝 YAML</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">🎯 CBA 22%</span>
            </div>
            </div><!-- /chapter-intro -->

            <div class="learning-objectives">
                <h4>🎯 What You'll Learn</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>✅ Master the 4 required top-level fields: apiVersion, kind, metadata, spec</li>
                    <li>✅ Understand every metadata field — name, annotations, labels, tags, links</li>
                    <li>✅ Know spec properties for ALL 7 documented entity kinds</li>
                    <li>✅ Use annotations to link entities to external systems</li>
                    <li>✅ Split or combine entities in one file with the <code>---</code> separator</li>
                    <li>✅ Validate a catalog-info.yaml before and after it's committed</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="cka-chapter-relevance">
                <span class="relevance-label">🎓 CBA Relevance</span>
                <div class="relevance-domains">
                    <span class="cka-domain-badge">Backstage Catalog <span class="cka-weight">22%</span></span>
