                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cka-exam-tip">
                <h5>🎯 The Most Hands-On Chapter for the CBA Exam</h5>
                <p>This chapter is the most literal, YAML-level test of the entity model taught in Chapter 8. You may be shown a YAML snippet and asked to identify what's missing or wrong.</p>
            </div>

            <h4>🧭 Section Map — the Chapter 9 Learning Arc</h4>
            <div class="diagram-container">
                <div class="diagram-title">Chapter 9 Roadmap — from the 4 required fields to a validated file</div>
<pre>
   9.1 STRUCTURE ──▶ 9.2 METADATA ──▶ 9.3 SPEC ──▶ 9.4 ANNOTATIONS ──▶ 9.5 MULTI-ENTITY ──▶ 9.6 VALIDATING
</pre>
            </div>
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Answers the question…</th><th>One-line takeaway</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><a href="#b-s9-1"><strong>9.1</strong> Structure</a></td><td>What must every file have?</td><td>4 required top-level fields — no exceptions.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><a href="#b-s9-2"><strong>9.2</strong> Metadata</a></td><td>What goes in the identity layer?</td><td>Only <code>name</code> is required; everything else is optional but valuable.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><a href="#b-s9-3"><strong>9.3</strong> Spec</a></td><td>What fields does MY kind need?</td><td>Every kind has a different spec shape.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><a href="#b-s9-4"><strong>9.4</strong> Annotations</a></td><td>How do I wire up external tools?</td><td>5 groups — core, Git, CI/CD, monitoring, Kubernetes.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><a href="#b-s9-5"><strong>9.5</strong> Multi-Entity Files</a></td><td>Can I define more than one entity per file?</td><td>Yes — with a <code>---</code> separator.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><a href="#b-s9-6"><strong>9.6</strong> Validating</a></td><td>How do I catch errors before they ship?</td><td>The ValidateEntity API, or ingestion logs after the fact.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <!-- ─────────── §9.1 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s9-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">9.1 catalog-info.yaml Structure — The 4 Required Fields</h3>
                <p>Every catalog-info.yaml MUST have exactly 4 top-level fields: <code>apiVersion</code>, <code>kind</code>, <code>metadata</code>, and <code>spec</code>. If any of these are missing, the entity will fail ingestion. <code>kind</code> must be one of <strong>9 valid values</strong>: Component, API, System, Domain, Resource, User, Group, Location, Template.</p>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Anatomy of catalog-info.yaml</div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: backstage.io/v1alpha1   <span class="comment">← 1️⃣ API VERSION (always this value)</span>
kind: Component                      <span class="comment">← 2️⃣ ENTITY KIND (Component|API|System|...)</span>
metadata:                            <span class="comment">← 3️⃣ IDENTITY (name, description, annotations)</span>
  name: jobpost                      <span class="comment">← REQUIRED: unique name per kind</span>
  description: "Job posting app"     <span class="comment"># Optional but recommended</span>
  annotations:                       <span class="comment"># Key-value pairs for integrations</span>
    github.com/project-slug: easypj/jobpost
  labels:                            <span class="comment"># Key-value for filtering</span>
    language: python
  tags: [django, recruitment]        <span class="comment"># Simple string tags</span>
  links:                             <span class="comment"># External URLs</span>
    - url: https://jobpost.easypj.com
      title: Production
spec:                                <span class="comment">← 4️⃣ TYPE-SPECIFIC PROPERTIES</span>
  type: service                      <span class="comment"># Depends on 'kind'</span>
  lifecycle: production
  owner: team-platform               <span class="comment"># REQUIRED for most kinds</span>
  system: easypj-system</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ─────────── §9.2 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s9-2">
                <h3 class="section-h">9.2 Metadata — The Identity Layer</h3>
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required?</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>Unique identifier per kind</td><td>jobpost</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>namespace</code></td><td>❌ No (default: "default")</td><td>Multi-tenant isolation. Separate entities by team/org</td><td>easypj-team</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>title</code></td><td>❌ No</td><td>Display name (differs from name)</td><td>Job Posting Service</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>❌ No (recommended)</td><td>Human-readable description</td><td>Recruitment management</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>labels</code></td><td>❌ No</td><td>Key-value pairs for filtering</td><td>language: python</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>tags</code></td><td>❌ No</td><td>Simple string tags</td><td>[django, backend]</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>annotations</code></td><td>❌ No (critical for integrations)</td><td>backstage.io/* for integrations</td><td>github.com/project-slug</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>links</code></td><td>❌ No</td><td>Array of external URLs</td><td>Prod URL, Dashboard, Docs</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box tip mb-0"><h5>💡 Labels vs Tags vs Annotations</h5><p class="mb-0"><strong>Labels</strong> are key-value pairs for filtering (e.g., <code>language: python</code> → find all Python services). <strong>Tags</strong> are simple strings for searching (e.g., <code>[django]</code> → quick search). <strong>Annotations</strong> are key-value pairs for integrations (e.g., <code>github.com/project-slug</code> → connects to GitHub repo). Labels filter, Tags search, Annotations integrate.</p></div>
            </section>

            <!-- ─────────── §9.3 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s9-3">
                <h3 class="section-h">9.3 Spec — Type-Specific Properties for Each Kind</h3>

                <div id="b-s9-3a"><h4>Component Spec</h4>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><h5>📦 Component Spec Fields</h5><p><code>type</code>: service|website|library|CLI<br><code>lifecycle</code>: experimental|production|deprecated<br><code>owner</code>: Group reference (required)<br><code>system</code>: System reference<br><code>subcomponentOf</code>: Parent component<br><code>providesApis</code>: APIs exposed<br><code>consumesApis</code>: APIs consumed<br><code>dependsOn</code>: Resources/components needed</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>📝 Example — jobpost Component</h5><pre><code class="language-yaml">spec:
  type: service
  lifecycle: production
  owner: team-platform
  system: easypj-system
  providesApis:
    - jobpost-api
  dependsOn:
    - resource:postgres-db
    - resource:redis-cache</code></pre></div>
                </div></div>

                <div id="b-s9-3b"><h4>API Spec</h4>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><h5>📡 API Spec Fields</h5><p><code>type</code>: openapi|asyncapi|graphql|grpc<br><code>lifecycle</code>: experimental|production|deprecated<br><code>owner</code>: Group reference (required)<br><code>system</code>: System reference<br><code>definition</code>: $text URL to API spec file</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>📝 Example — jobpost-api</h5><pre><code class="language-yaml">spec:
  type: openapi
  lifecycle: production
  owner: team-platform
  system: easypj-system
  definition:
    $text: https://github.com/easypj/
           jobpost/blob/main/openapi.yaml</code></pre></div>
                </div></div>

                <div id="b-s9-3c"><h4>Resource Spec</h4>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><h5>💾 Resource Spec Fields</h5><p><code>type</code>: database|s3-bucket|pubsub-topic|cache|queue<br><code>owner</code>: Group reference (required)<br><code>system</code>: System reference<br><code>dependsOn</code>: Other resources<br><code>dependencyOf</code>: Components using this</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>📝 Example — postgres-db</h5><pre><code class="language-yaml">spec:
  type: database
  owner: team-platform
  system: easypj-system
  dependencyOf:
    - component:jobpost</code></pre></div>
                </div></div>

                <div id="b-s9-3d"><h4>System &amp; Domain Spec</h4>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><h5>🖥️ System Spec</h5><p><code>owner</code>: Group reference (required)<br><code>domain</code>: Domain reference<br>Groups Components + Resources together.</p><pre><code class="language-yaml">spec:
  owner: team-platform
  domain: hr-domain</code></pre></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>🏢 Domain Spec</h5><p><code>owner</code>: Group reference (required)<br>Organizational containers — simplest spec.<br>Groups Systems under business areas.</p><pre><code class="language-yaml">spec:
  owner: engineering-leadership</code></pre></div>
                </div></div>

                <div id="b-s9-3e"><h4>User &amp; Group Spec</h4>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><h5>👤 User Spec</h5><p><code>profile</code>: email, displayName, picture<br><code>memberOf</code>: Groups the user belongs to</p><pre><code class="language-yaml">spec:
  profile:
    email: jane@easypj.com
