            <details class="uth">
                <summary>Under the Hood — the full set of clusterLocatorMethods, and pinning to one cluster</summary>
                <div class="uth-body">
                    <p><code>clusterLocatorMethods</code> supports more than the static <code>config</code> type easypj uses.</p>
                    <h5>① The 4 clusterLocatorMethods Types</h5>
                    <pre class="uth-diagram">
config             → static, hand-listed clusters (easypj's method)
catalog            → derive clusters from Catalog entities instead of static config
gke                → auto-discover Google Kubernetes Engine clusters
localKubectlProxy  → use your local kubectl proxy (development only)
                    </pre>
                    <h5>② Pinning to One Cluster</h5>
                    <p>The <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-cluster</code> annotation lets one entity pin itself to exactly one named cluster — used together with the <code>singleTenant</code> serviceLocatorMethod when Backstage must be told which configured cluster an entity's resources live in, rather than searching every configured cluster.</p>
                    <div class="uth-callout mb-0"><strong>🔑 multiTenant + no pin = search everywhere; singleTenant + kubernetes-cluster = search exactly one place.</strong> Pick multiTenant unless you have a specific reason to restrict the search.</div>
                </div>
            </details>

