                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q7</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">Where does Backstage get K8s resource data — from a cache or live?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p><strong>Live</strong> — the K8s plugin calls the K8s API server directly each time you view the entity's K8s tab. No built-in caching.</p>
                        <pre class="uth-diagram">
View K8s tab  →  Backstage backend  →  K8s API server (fresh call, every time)
                        </pre>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>Pros: always accurate. Cons: adds latency, and a slow/unreachable K8s API makes the tab hang. Redis caching can be added but isn't built-in.</p></div>
                    </details>
