            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch12-uth"></span>
            <details class="uth">
                <summary>Under the Hood — every action is the same ctx.input → handler → ctx.output contract</summary>
                <div class="uth-body">
                    <p>Every action registered with the scaffolder backend is, under the hood, just a function that reads <code>ctx.input</code>, does its work, and calls <code>ctx.output(name, value)</code> to publish results.</p>
                    <h5>① One Shared Contract, One Shared Workspace</h5>
                    <pre class="uth-diagram">
scaffolder engine strings actions together in spec.steps order
                ↓
each action shares ONE temp workspace directory
                ↓
fetch:template WRITES into it  →  publish:github later READS from it
                    </pre>
                    <div class="uth-callout mb-0"><strong>🔑 Because every action shares this one interface, a custom action like <code>easypj:notify-slack</code> (§12.3) can sit in the same <code>steps:</code> list as a built-in action like <code>publish:github</code></strong> with zero special-casing by the engine.</div>
                </div>
            </details>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch12-takeaways"></span>
            <div class="key-takeaways">
                <h4>🔑 Key Takeaways</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>The built-in action catalog covers</strong> fetching (fetch:template, fetch:plain, fetch:cookiecutter), publishing (publish:github/gitlab/bitbucket/azure), and catalog registration (catalog:register, catalog:write), plus small file utilities (fs:delete, roadiehq:utils:fs:replace).</li>
                    <li><strong>Every action's OUTPUT is addressable by later steps</strong> as <code>${{ steps.id.output.field }}</code> — the wiring that lets register reach back to what publish produced.</li>
                    <li><strong>The skeleton/ directory is what fetch:template actually copies;</strong> every file inside it can use <code>{{ values.X }}</code> placeholders.</li>
                    <li><strong><code>spec.output.links/text</code> is what renders on the scaffolder Task completion page</strong> — skip it and the user sees only raw step logs.</li>
                    <li><strong>A custom action is built with <code>createTemplateAction</code>,</strong> declares an input schema, and calls <code>ctx.output(...)</code> — the same contract as any built-in.</li>
                    <li><strong>Reach for a custom action only when the built-in catalog has no action for the job</strong> — most templates need zero custom code.</li>
                    <li><strong>The 3 most common template failures:</strong> a missing required parameter, a wrong/unregistered templateRef, or a typo'd <code>{{ values.X }}</code> placeholder left literally in the output.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch12-gotchas"></span>
            <div class="cka-gotcha">
                <h5>⚠️ Common Gotchas &amp; Misconceptions</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Confusing <code>catalog:write</code> with <code>catalog:register</code></strong> — <code>catalog:write</code> only writes a YAML file to disk, it does NOT register anything in the Catalog (§12.1).</li>
                    <li><strong>Assuming a custom action needs to reinvent file-copying</strong> — most custom actions should call an external system (Slack, ticketing, a check) and let the built-ins handle files/repos/catalog (§12.3).</li>
                    <li><strong>Not marking a custom action's input properties as <code>required</code></strong> — an unvalidated <code>ctx.input.X</code> can be undefined at runtime and crash the handler (§12.3).</li>
                    <li><strong>Missing <code>rules: [{allow: [Template]}]</code></strong> on the catalog.locations entry that points at a template — a template not marked as such won't run (§12.4).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch12-speed"></span>
            <div class="cka-speed-tip">
                <h5>⚡ Speed Tips</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Validate template.yaml syntax</strong> before running it instead of debugging blind inside the Create wizard.</li>
                    <li><strong>Run with <code>BACKSTAGE_LOG_LEVEL=debug</code></strong> when a step's output doesn't seem to flow into the next step — the debug log shows the resolved <code>{{ steps.* }}</code> values.</li>
                    <li><strong>Check the "IF YOU NEED TO... REACH FOR..." decision table (§12.3)</strong> before writing any custom action.</li>
