                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">Name 5 built-in template actions and what each does.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td><code>fetch:template</code></td><td>Copy skeleton with placeholders</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>publish:github</code></td><td>Create GitHub repo + push code</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>catalog:register</code></td><td>Register in Catalog</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>fetch:plain</code></td><td>Copy files from URL</td></tr>
                                <tr><td><code>fs:delete</code></td><td>Delete files during template run</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>The core 3 (fetch:template, publish:github, catalog:register) appear in nearly every template. The exam may ask "Which action would you use to..." scenarios.</p></div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">What goes inside the ./skeleton directory?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>All boilerplate files for the new project — using <code>${{ values.PARAM }}</code> for customization.</p>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>catalog-info.yaml</td><td>Registers the service</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Dockerfile</td><td>Containerizes it</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>.github/workflows/ci.yml</td><td>Automates testing/deployment</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>k8s/deployment.yaml</td><td>Defines the deployment</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>The skeleton is the blueprint for every new project — its placeholders ensure each generated project is unique.</p></div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">How do you create a custom template action?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>Use <code>createTemplateAction()</code> from <code>@backstage/plugin-scaffolder-node</code>.</p>
                        <div class="code-block-wrapper"><div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">the 3 required parts</span></div><pre><code class="language-typescript">createTemplateAction({
  id: 'unique-id',
  schema: { input: { required: [...], properties: {...} } },
  async handler(ctx) { ctx.output('field', value); },
});</code></pre></div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>The <code>id</code> must be unique across all registered actions. The handler receives <code>ctx</code> with input, logger, and workspace path.</p></div>
                    </details>
                </div>

