                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">A developer uses <code>catalog:write</code> expecting it to register their new Component in the Catalog. It doesn't show up. Why?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p><code>catalog:write</code> only writes a YAML file to disk — it does NOT register anything. They needed <code>catalog:register</code> instead.</p>
                        <table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Registers in Catalog?</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                            <tr><td>catalog:write</td><td>❌ No — writes YAML only</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>catalog:register</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr>
                        </tbody></table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>§12's Gotcha — this exact name-confusion is a named exam trap.</p></div>
