            <section class="section-block" id="b-s13-3">
                <h3 class="section-h">13.3 Template: Database Migration Job</h3>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><h5>🗄️ Job vs Service</h5><p><strong>Service:</strong> Runs continuously, handles requests.<br><strong>Job:</strong> Runs once to completion, then stops.<br>Migrations must run BEFORE new version deploys — Jobs are perfect for this.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>📋 What It Generates</h5><p>Dockerfile with migration scripts, K8s Job manifest (backoffLimit, ttlSecondsAfterFinished), CronJob variant for scheduled runs, DB credential config, catalog-info.yaml (type: job).</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Migration Job vs CronJob</div>
<pre>
  K8s JOB (Run Once)                      K8s CRONJOB (Scheduled)
  ┌──────────────────────┐               ┌──────────────────────┐
  │ apiVersion: batch/v1 │               │ apiVersion: batch/v1 │
  │ kind: Job            │               │ kind: CronJob        │
  │ backoffLimit: 3      │               │ schedule: "0 2 * * *"│
  │ ttlSecondsAfter: 300 │               │ jobTemplate: {...}   │
  │                      │               │                      │
  │ Use: CI/CD pipelines │               │ Use: Nightly cleanup │
  │ before deploy        │               │ data sync, backups   │
  └──────────────────────┘               └──────────────────────┘
</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">templates/db-migration-job/template.yaml — complete</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: scaffolder.backstage.io/v1beta3
kind: Template
metadata:
  name: db-migration-job
  title: New Database Migration Job
  tags: [django, database, k8s-job]
spec:
  owner: team-platform
  type: service
  parameters:
    - title: Job Details
      required: [name, targetService]
      properties:
        name: { type: string }
        targetService: { type: string, ui:field: EntityPicker }
        isCronJob: { type: boolean, default: false }
  steps:
    - id: fetch
      action: fetch:template
      input: { url: ./skeleton }
      <span class="comment"># skeleton contains: k8s/job.yaml (or cronjob.yaml if isCronJob)</span>
    - id: publish
      action: publish:github
      input: { repoUrl: "github.com?owner=easypj&repo=${{ parameters.name }}" }
    - id: register
      action: catalog:register
      input: { repoContentsUrl: "${{ steps.publish.output.repoContentsUrl }}" }</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ─────────── §13.4 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s13-4">
                <h3 class="section-h">13.4 Template: Infrastructure as Code</h3>
                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Terraform Template — File Structure</div>
<pre>
  templates/infra-as-code/skeleton/
  ├── main.tf          ← Resource definitions (compute, networking, DB)
  ├── variables.tf     ← Parameterized inputs with defaults
  ├── outputs.tf       ← Connection strings, IPs, endpoints
  ├── backend.tf       ← Remote state (S3/GCS/Azure Blob)
  ├── providers.tf     ← AWS/GCP/Azure provider config
  └── catalog-info.yaml ← Registered as kind: Resource

  CI PIPELINE:
  terraform fmt → terraform validate → terraform plan
  (apply runs separately after human approval)
</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">templates/infra-as-code/template.yaml — complete</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: scaffolder.backstage.io/v1beta3
kind: Template
metadata:
  name: infra-as-code
  title: New Terraform Infrastructure
  tags: [terraform, infrastructure]
spec:
  owner: team-platform
  type: resource
  parameters:
    - title: Infrastructure Details
      required: [name, cloudProvider]
      properties:
        name: { type: string }
        cloudProvider: { type: string, enum: [aws, gcp, azure] }
  steps:
    - id: fetch
      action: fetch:template
      input: { url: ./skeleton }
      <span class="comment"># skeleton contains: main.tf, variables.tf, outputs.tf, backend.tf</span>
    - id: publish
      action: publish:github
      input: { repoUrl: "github.com?owner=easypj&repo=${{ parameters.name }}" }
    - id: register
      action: catalog:register
      input: { repoContentsUrl: "${{ steps.publish.output.repoContentsUrl }}" }</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="info-box note mb-0"><h5>🔑 CBA Key Concept — Terraform State</h5><p class="mb-0">Terraform state must be stored <strong>remotely</strong> (S3/GCS/Azure Blob), never locally. The <code>backend.tf</code> file configures this. Remote state enables team collaboration and prevents state conflicts. The CBA may test: "Where should Terraform state be stored?" Answer: remote backend, not local files.</p></div>
            </section>

