            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch17-uth"></span>
            <details class="uth">
                <summary>Under the Hood — the one shared wiring pattern behind all 6 plugins</summary>
                <div class="uth-body">
                    <p>Every plugin in this chapter follows the exact same wiring pattern.</p>
                    <h5>① Two Pieces, Two Files, One Card</h5>
                    <pre class="uth-diagram">
app-config.yaml   →  the SECRET/ENDPOINT (integrations.github, proxy.endpoints,
                      pagerDuty.apiToken, sentry.organization, slack.webhookUrl)
                                    +
catalog-info.yaml →  the ENTITY-SPECIFIC IDENTIFIER (metadata.annotations)
                                    ↓
                      Card only renders when BOTH pieces are present
                    </pre>
                    <div class="uth-callout mb-0"><strong>🔑 The plugin reads the annotation to know WHICH external resource to query, and app-config.yaml to know HOW to authenticate.</strong> Grafana (§17.3) additionally never talks to the browser directly — it's routed through app-config.yaml's <code>proxy.endpoints</code> so the Grafana token never reaches the client.</div>
                </div>
            </details>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch17-takeaways"></span>
            <div class="key-takeaways">
                <h4>🔑 Key Takeaways</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>All 6 integration plugins share one pattern:</strong> app-config.yaml holds the secret/endpoint, catalog-info.yaml's metadata.annotations turns the card ON for a specific entity.</li>
                    <li><strong>GitHub Integration needs <code>integrations.github</code></strong> (app-config.yaml) <strong>+ <code>github.com/project-slug</code></strong> (annotation).</li>
                    <li><strong>CI/CD cards</strong> (GitHub Actions, Jenkins, ArgoCD) each have their own annotation; ArgoCD additionally needs <code>argocd.baseUrl</code>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Monitoring plugins route browser calls through a backend proxy entry,</strong> not directly to the external service.</li>
                    <li><strong>PagerDuty/Sentry need BOTH an app-config.yaml token/org AND an entity annotation</strong> — the token alone shows nothing.</li>
                    <li><strong>Slack has no entity-page card</strong> — it's used by Scaffolder/custom actions (§12.3) to post deploy alerts to a channel.</li>
                    <li><strong>If no plugin exists for a tool you need,</strong> that's the "build a custom plugin" case covered in Chapter 18 §18.1.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch17-gotchas"></span>
            <div class="cka-gotcha">
                <h5>⚠️ Common Gotchas &amp; Misconceptions</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Forgetting the entity-level annotation</strong> — the app-config.yaml token alone will NOT make a card appear (Under the Hood §①).</li>
                    <li><strong>Mixing up WHERE config belongs:</strong> secrets/endpoints in app-config.yaml, entity identifiers in catalog-info.yaml annotations.</li>
                    <li><strong>Assuming Grafana talks directly to the browser</strong> — it's proxied through app-config.yaml's <code>proxy.endpoints</code> (§17.3).</li>
                    <li><strong>Confusing <code>jenkins.io/job-full-name</code> (Jenkins) with <code>github.com/project-slug</code> (GitHub Actions)</strong> — separate annotations for separate cards (§17.2).</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <span class="ch-jump" id="b-ch17-speed"></span>
            <div class="cka-speed-tip">
                <h5>⚡ Speed Tips</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Copy the annotation block from §17.2 as a template</strong> — swap only the value per entity.</li>
                    <li><strong>Keep every plugin token as <code>${ENV_VAR}</code></strong> in app-config.yaml, never hardcoded.</li>
                    <li><strong>When a card doesn't render, check the annotation FIRST, then the app-config.yaml section</strong> — in that order.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

