            <!-- ─────────── §18.5 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s18-5">
                <h3 class="section-h">18.5 Testing Custom Plugins</h3>
                <p>Test plugins with: (1) <strong>Jest unit tests</strong> for components and API logic, (2) <strong>Integration tests</strong> for full plugin workflows, (3) <strong>Manual testing</strong> with <code>yarn dev</code> — the plugin appears in the sidebar and can be tested interactively.</p>

                <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Test Layer</th><th>Tool</th><th>What It Tests</th><th>Command</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>Unit</strong></td><td>Jest + <code>renderInTestApp()</code></td><td>Individual components, API functions, utility logic</td><td><code>yarn test</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Integration</strong></td><td>Jest + Supertest</td><td>Full plugin workflow: API call → DB query → response</td><td><code>yarn test --integration</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Manual</strong></td><td><code>yarn dev</code> + Browser</td><td>Real UI rendering, sidebar visibility, route navigation, API calls</td><td><code>yarn dev</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>E2E</strong></td><td>Playwright / Cypress</td><td>Full user journey: click sidebar → load page → interact with cards</td><td><code>yarn test:e2e</code></td></tr>
                </tbody></table></div>

                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">plugins/easypj-dashboard/src/components/DashboardPage.test.tsx</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-typescript">import { renderInTestApp } from '@backstage/test-utils';
import { DashboardPage } from './DashboardPage';

describe('DashboardPage', () => {
  it('renders job stats', async () => {
    const { getByText } = await renderInTestApp(&lt;DashboardPage /&gt;);
    expect(getByText(/active/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});

// Run: yarn test --testPathPattern=easypj-dashboard</code></pre>
                </div>

                <div class="card-grid cols-3">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><div class="card-icon-lg">🧪</div><h5>Jest Unit Tests</h5><p>Use <code>renderInTestApp()</code> — Backstage's own test wrapper, not plain <code>render()</code>. It provides the App context (theme, routing, APIs) a real plugin component expects.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🔗</div><h5>Integration Tests</h5><p>Test the full stack: frontend → API proxy → backend → database. Use Supertest for HTTP assertions against backend routes.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">👁️</div><h5>Manual Testing</h5><p>Run <code>yarn dev</code>, navigate to <code>localhost:3000/easypj-dashboard</code>, verify cards render with real data from a running database.</p></div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box tip mb-0"><h5>💡 CBA Testing Tip</h5><p class="mb-0">The CBA expects you to know the 3 testing layers (unit, integration, manual) and which tool each uses. <code>renderInTestApp()</code> from <code>@backstage/test-utils</code> is the standard way to unit-test a plugin component — not a plain React Testing Library <code>render()</code>.</p></div>
