            <!-- ─────────── §18.6 (NEW — from Backstage.txt, no HTML equivalent existed) ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s18-6">
                <h3 class="section-h">18.6 Making Changes to React Code in the Backstage App</h3>
                <p>This is <strong>DIFFERENT</strong> from building a plugin (§18.1-18.4): here you edit the App SHELL itself — <code>packages/app/src/App.tsx</code> and <code>Root.tsx</code>. Common app-shell changes: add a route, add/remove a sidebar item, change the homepage, wire up a custom theme (see Chapter 4 §4.5). <code>App.tsx</code> wires plugins + routes together; <code>Root.tsx</code> defines the persistent shell (sidebar, header) that wraps every page.</p>

                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>What You Edit It For</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><code>packages/app/src/App.tsx</code></td><td>Register plugins/APIs, define &lt;Routes&gt;, set the homepage component</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>packages/app/src/components/Root/Root.tsx</code></td><td>Sidebar items, header, persistent layout</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>packages/app/src/apis.ts</code></td><td>Wire up ApiRef implementations</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>packages/app/src/components/</code></td><td>Your own shared React components used across multiple pages</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">Adding a new route — real diff on App.tsx</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-typescript">import { EasypjDashboardPage } from '@internal/plugin-easypj-dashboard';

const routes = (
  &lt;FlatRoutes&gt;
    &lt;Route path='/catalog' element={&lt;CatalogIndexPage /&gt;} /&gt;
    &lt;Route path='/create' element={&lt;ScaffolderPage /&gt;} /&gt;
+   &lt;Route path='/easypj-dashboard' element={&lt;EasypjDashboardPage /&gt;} /&gt;
  &lt;/FlatRoutes&gt;
