            <section class="section-block" id="b-s19-3">
                <h3 class="section-h">19.3 Docker Image for Backstage</h3>
                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Multi-Stage Dockerfile — easypj customization</div>
<pre><code class="language-bash"># Stage 1: Build
FROM node:18-bookworm-slim AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json yarn.lock ./
RUN yarn install --frozen-lockfile --production=false
COPY . .
RUN yarn tsc && yarn build

# Stage 2: Production (smaller image)
FROM node:18-bookworm-slim AS runtime
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=build /app/packages/backend/dist ./dist
COPY --from=build /app/packages/backend/package.json ./
COPY --from=build /app/node_modules ./node_modules
ENV NODE_ENV=production
EXPOSE 7007
CMD ["node", "packages/backend", "--config", "app-config.yaml"]</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><h5>Multi-Stage Build</h5><p>Stage 1 installs ALL dependencies (including devDependencies for TypeScript), compiles, and builds. Stage 2 copies only the compiled output and production dependencies. This keeps the final image small (~300MB vs ~1.5GB).</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>Image Tagging Strategy</h5><p>Use semantic versioning: <code>v1.2.3</code>. Tag each build with the Git commit SHA: <code>registry.easypj.com/backstage:v1.2.3-abc1234</code>. This ensures every deployment is traceable to a specific commit.</p></div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ─────────── §19.4 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s19-4">
                <h3 class="section-h">19.4 Kubernetes Manifests</h3>

                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ The 4 Fields That MUST Point at the Ingress Host</h5>
                    <p class="mb-0">Inside the mounted <code>app-config.yaml</code>, four fields must all resolve to the externally-reachable Ingress host (e.g. <code>backstage.easypj.com</code>) — <strong><code>app.baseUrl</code></strong>, <strong><code>backend.baseUrl</code></strong>, <strong><code>backend.listen.port</code></strong>, and <strong><code>backend.cors.origin</code></strong>. Get any of these wrong and Pods report Healthy while the browser silently fails to load data — the "it's running but it's broken" trap.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Must resolve to…</th><th>If wrong…</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><code>app.baseUrl</code></td><td>Ingress host (browser-facing URL)</td><td>Frontend links/redirects break</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>backend.baseUrl</code></td><td>Ingress host</td><td>Frontend can't find the backend</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>backend.listen.port</code></td><td>7007 (container port)</td><td>Backend never starts listening</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>backend.cors.origin</code></td><td>Ingress host</td><td>Browser requests blocked by CORS</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Complete K8s Deployment YAML for Backstage</div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: backstage
  namespace: backstage
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: backstage
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: backstage
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: backstage
        image: registry.easypj.com/backstage:v1.0
        ports:
          - containerPort: 7007
        env:
          - name: POSTGRES_HOST
            valueFrom:
              secretKeyRef:
                name: backstage-secrets
                key: postgres-host
          - name: POSTGRES_PASSWORD
            valueFrom:
              secretKeyRef:
                name: backstage-secrets
                key: postgres-password
          - name: GITHUB_TOKEN
            valueFrom:
              secretKeyRef:
                name: backstage-secrets
                key: github-token
        volumeMounts:
          - name: app-config
            mountPath: /app/app-config.yaml
            subPath: app-config.yaml
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: "512Mi"
            cpu: "500m"
          limits:
            memory: "2Gi"
            cpu: "2000m"
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /healthcheck
            port: 7007
          initialDelaySeconds: 30
          periodSeconds: 10
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /healthcheck
            port: 7007
          initialDelaySeconds: 10
          periodSeconds: 5
      volumes:
        - name: app-config
          configMap:
            name: backstage-config</code></pre>
                </div>

                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>Service + Ingress</h5><p>ClusterIP Service on port 7007. Ingress with TLS termination and host: <code>backstage.easypj.com</code>. Annotations for cert-manager if using Let's Encrypt.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>ConfigMap + Secret</h5><p>ConfigMap stores app-config.yaml (mounted as file). Secret stores: POSTGRES_HOST, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, GITHUB_TOKEN. Never put secrets in ConfigMap!</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><h5>PersistentVolumeClaim</h5><p>Used for TechDocs cache if using local publisher. In production with cloud publisher (GCS/S3/Azure), PVC is not needed for TechDocs — only for PostgreSQL data.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><h5>Namespace</h5><p>Every manifest above targets the <code>backstage</code> namespace — created once, up front, with <code>kubectl create namespace backstage</code> (or via Helm's <code>--create-namespace</code> flag, §19.5).</p></div>
                </div>
            </section>

