                <h4>🧠 Chapter 19 — Lab Q&amp;A · Concept Check (10)</h4>
                <p class="section-lead">Quick recall of Docker builds, K8s manifests, and Helm deployment — 10 questions, each with a full answer &amp; explanation.</p>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">Why should Backstage use PostgreSQL instead of SQLite in production?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>SQLite only supports a single writer — with 3 Backstage replicas on K8s, concurrent writes would cause data corruption. PostgreSQL handles concurrent connections from multiple pods safely and is the only supported production database for Backstage.</p>
                        <table><thead><tr><th>Database</th><th>Concurrent writers?</th><th>Safe with 3 replicas?</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                            <tr><td>SQLite</td><td>❌ Single-writer lock</td><td>❌ No</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>PostgreSQL</td><td>✅ MVCC concurrency</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr>
                        </tbody></table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>This is the #1 reason you can't run SQLite in production with multiple pods. The CBA tests this as a key production requirement — always PostgreSQL on K8s.</p></div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">What does a multi-stage Dockerfile achieve for Backstage?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>Stage 1 (build): installs ALL deps, compiles TypeScript, builds the app. Stage 2 (runtime): copies only compiled output + production deps. Result: smaller image (~300MB vs ~1.5GB), faster pulls, smaller attack surface.</p>
                        <div class="code-block-wrapper"><div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">2-stage pattern</span></div><pre><code class="language-bash">FROM node:18-bookworm-slim AS build   # 1.5GB — compilers, devDeps
...
FROM node:18-bookworm-slim AS runtime # 300MB — production only</code></pre></div>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>Multi-stage builds solve the "fat image" problem. Benefits: faster deploys (smaller pull), fewer CVEs (fewer packages), lower storage costs. CBA: know the 2-stage pattern and its benefits.</p></div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">Where should you store app-config.yaml in a K8s deployment?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>In a <strong>ConfigMap</strong>, mounted as a file in the pod. Secrets (DB passwords, tokens) should be in a separate Secret resource, not in the ConfigMap.</p>
                        <table><thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>Holds</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                            <tr><td>ConfigMap</td><td>Non-sensitive config (app-config.yaml)</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Secret</td><td>Sensitive data (passwords, tokens)</td></tr>
                        </tbody></table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>CBA: NEVER put passwords in ConfigMap. ConfigMap changes require pod restart to take effect (unless using subPath mount or reloader).</p></div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">What Kubernetes resources are needed to deploy Backstage in production?</div>
