            <div class="cka-exam-tip">
                <h5>🎯 CBA Exam Tip — Annotation-to-LABEL, Never Entity Name</h5>
                <p>The CBA frequently asks: "How does Backstage know which K8s resources belong to an entity?" The precise answer: the <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-id</code> annotation on the entity's catalog-info.yaml must match a <strong>label</strong> on the K8s Deployment — the plugin never looks at the entity's own name or the Deployment's name. Forget the label on the Deployment and the K8s tab stays empty even with a perfectly correct annotation. Also know: <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-namespace</code> overrides the default namespace, and <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-cluster</code> pins an entity to one cluster under <code>singleTenant</code> (first introduced in Chapter 10's clusterLocatorMethods discussion).</p>
