            <section class="section-block" id="b-s20-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">20.1 K8s Plugin Architecture — How It Connects</h3>
                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">K8s Plugin — Frontend + Backend Architecture</div>
<pre>
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                     K8s PLUGIN — DUAL LAYER                                │
  │                                                                          │
  │  🖥️ FRONTEND (Browser) — @backstage/plugin-kubernetes                     │
  │  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
  │  │  Entity Page → "KUBERNETES" Tab                                     │  │
  │  │  ┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐                │  │
  │  │  │ Deployments  │ │    Pods      │ │  Services    │                │  │
  │  │  │ jobpost: 3/3 │ │ ✅ Running   │ │ :8000 (TCP)  │                │  │
  │  │  └──────────────┘ └──────────────┘ └──────────────┘                │  │
  │  └──────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────┘  │
  │                                 │ REST: /api/kubernetes/services/:ref    │
  │  ⚙️ BACKEND (Node.js) — @backstage/plugin-kubernetes-backend             │
  │  ┌──────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────┐  │
  │  │  KubernetesServiceApi                                               │  │
  │  │  • Reads entity annotations (kubernetes-id, namespace, selector)    │  │
  │  │  • Calls K8s API Server (get/list/watch resources)                  │  │
  │  │  • Returns merged results to frontend                               │  │
  │  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Correction — It's Annotation-to-LABEL, Never Entity Name</h5>
                    <p class="mb-0">The plugin does <strong>NOT</strong> match on the catalog entity's name, and it does not match the annotation against the Deployment's <em>name</em> either — it matches the <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-id</code> annotation value against a <strong>label</strong> on the running Deployment. Forget the label on the Deployment and the Kubernetes tab stays empty even with a perfectly correct annotation on the entity.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">How kubernetes-id Resolves to Real Pods</div>
<pre>
  catalog-info.yaml                          Running in the cluster
    metadata:                                    Deployment "jobpost"
      annotations:                                 labels:
        backstage.io/kubernetes-id: jobpost -->      backstage.io/kubernetes-id: jobpost

  The plugin does NOT match on entity name — it matches ONLY on this
  annotation-to-label pair. Forget the label on the Deployment and the
  Kubernetes tab stays empty even with a perfectly correct annotation.
</pre>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box note mb-0"><h5>🔑 3 Annotations Drive Discovery</h5><p class="mb-0">Backstage reads 3 annotations from the entity: <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-id</code> (matched against a Deployment LABEL, not a name), <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-namespace</code> (scope to specific namespace), <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-label-selector</code> (label-based query). The K8s API is queried with these filters, and results appear as cards on the entity's K8s tab.</p></div>
            </section>

            <!-- ─────────── §20.2 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s20-2">
                <h3 class="section-h">20.2 Multi-Cluster Setup — Connecting Multiple K8s Clusters</h3>
                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Multi-Cluster Architecture</div>
<pre>
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                         BACKSTAGE MULTI-CLUSTER                            │
  │                                                                          │
  │  ┌──────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────┐      │
  │  │ ☸️ easypj-prod    │   │ ☸️ easypj-staging │   │ ☸️ easypj-dev     │      │
  │  │ URL: k8s-prod...  │   │ URL: k8s-stage... │   │ URL: k8s-dev...   │      │
  │  │ Auth: SA Token A  │   │ Auth: SA Token B  │   │ Auth: OIDC        │      │
  │  └────────┬─────────┘   └────────┬─────────┘   └────────┬─────────┘      │
  │           │                      │                      │                 │
  │           └──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┘                 │
  │                                  │                                        │
  │                    ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐                          │
  │                    │       BACKSTAGE           │                          │
  │                    │  Queries ALL clusters     │                          │
  │                    │  Merges results by name   │                          │
  │                    └───────────────────────────┘                          │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">app-config.yaml — multi-cluster</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">kubernetes:
  serviceLocatorMethod: { type: multiTenant }
  clusterLocatorMethods:
    - type: config
      clusters:
        - name: easypj-prod
          url: https://k8s-prod.easypj.com
          authProvider: serviceAccount
          serviceAccountToken: ${K8S_PROD_TOKEN}
        - name: easypj-staging
          url: https://k8s-staging.easypj.com
          authProvider: serviceAccount
          serviceAccountToken: ${K8S_STAGING_TOKEN}</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="info-box tip">
                    <h5>💡 CBA Tip — the Real 4 Cluster Locator Methods</h5>
                    <p class="mb-0">Besides <code>config</code> (manual listing, the most commonly tested), Backstage supports <code>gke</code> (auto-discovers Google clusters), <code>catalog</code> (discovers clusters that are themselves catalog entities), and <code>localKubectlProxy</code> (dev-only, uses your local kubectl config). <strong><code>eks</code> and <code>aks</code> are NOT locator method types</strong> — they're <code>authProvider</code> values used for per-cluster authentication (Chapter 10 introduced this same 4-way <code>clusterLocatorMethods</code> breakdown).</p>
                </div>
                <div class="info-box note mb-0"><h5>🔑 Single-Cluster Pinning</h5><p class="mb-0">When <code>serviceLocatorMethod</code> is <code>singleTenant</code>, tag the entity with <code>backstage.io/kubernetes-cluster</code> to pin it to one specific cluster instead of fanning the query out to all of them — useful once you have dozens of clusters and know exactly where a given service lives.</p></div>
            </section>

