            <section class="section-block" id="b-s25-2">
                <h3 class="section-h">25.2 GitHub Actions Integration</h3>

                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ Correction — Moved to @backstage-community Scope</h5>
                    <p class="mb-0">The GitHub Actions plugin moved from the <code>@backstage/*</code> scope to <strong><code>@backstage-community/*</code></strong> in the April 2024 community-plugins migration — this renamed the packages, not just moved a repo. The current, correct package is <code>@backstage-community/plugin-github-actions</code> (frontend) and its matching backend package.</p>
                </div>

                <div id="b-s25-2a">
                    <h4>25.2a Workflow Configuration</h4>
                    <p>Install <code>@backstage-community/plugin-github-actions</code> in both <code>packages/app</code> and <code>packages/backend</code>. Add the <code>github.com/project-slug</code> annotation to entity YAML. Backstage auto-discovers workflow runs and displays status, logs, and duration on the entity's CI/CD card.</p>

                    <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                        <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">Install — the correct, current package</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-bash">yarn --cwd packages/app add @backstage-community/plugin-github-actions</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Location</th><th>What to Add</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                        <tr><td><strong>Frontend</strong></td><td><code>packages/app/package.json</code></td><td><code>"@backstage-community/plugin-github-actions"</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>Frontend</strong></td><td><code>packages/app/src/components/catalog/EntityPage.tsx</code></td><td><code>&lt;EntityGithubActionsContent /&gt;</code> in the CI/CD tab</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>Backend</strong></td><td><code>packages/backend/package.json</code></td><td><code>"@backstage-community/plugin-github-actions-backend"</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>Entity</strong></td><td><code>catalog-info.yaml</code></td><td><code>github.com/project-slug: easypj/jobpost</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>Config</strong></td><td><code>app-config.yaml</code></td><td><code>integrations.github[].token: ${GITHUB_TOKEN}</code></td></tr>
                    </tbody></table></div>

                    <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                        <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">catalog-info.yaml — Entity with GitHub Actions annotation</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: backstage.io/v1alpha1
kind: Component
metadata:
  name: jobpost
  description: Django job posting application
  annotations:
    # 🔑 This single annotation is enough — the plugin discovers
    # workflow runs automatically via the GitHub API
    github.com/project-slug: easypj/jobpost
    backstage.io/techdocs-ref: dir:.
spec:
  type: service
  lifecycle: production
  owner: easypj-team
  system: recruitment-platform</code></pre>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div id="b-s25-2b">
                    <h4>25.2b Viewing Runs in Backstage</h4>
                    <p>The GitHub Actions tab on the entity page shows: <strong>recent workflow runs</strong>, <strong>status</strong> (✅ pass / ❌ fail / 🔄 running), <strong>trigger type</strong> (push / PR / schedule), <strong>duration</strong>, and <strong>links to detailed logs</strong> on GitHub.</p>

