                <h4>🔑 Key Takeaways</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>CI/CD visibility means build/deploy status, recent runs and deep links</strong> surfaced right on the entity page (§25.1).</li>
                    <li><strong>GitHub Actions and Jenkins plugins both moved</strong> from the @backstage scope to @backstage-community in the April 2024 community-plugins migration (§25.2, §25.3).</li>
                    <li><strong>There is no first-party GitLab plugin</strong> — the Backstage plugin directory points to @immobiliarelabs/backstage-plugin-gitlab (+ its backend package) instead (§25.4).</li>
                    <li><strong>The argocd plugin block is SHARED</strong> between GitOps deployment status (Chapter 21) and CI/CD visibility (§25.5) — configure it once.</li>
                    <li><strong>A single aggregated card (§25.6)</strong> combining GithubActionsCard + ArgoCdCard + KubernetesCard beats four separate dashboard tabs.</li>
                    <li><strong>Every CI/CD card follows the same shape:</strong> annotation on the entity (lookup key) + credentials in central config, never on the entity itself.</li>
                    <li><strong>The Backstage proxy keeps every CI/CD auth token server-side</strong> — the frontend only ever sees rendered data, never credentials.</li>
                </ul>
