                <div class="exam-question-item"><span class="eq-number">Q2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">easypj's Backstage rollout has maxUnavailable: 0 but no readinessProbe defined. During a deploy, users briefly see errors. Why didn't maxUnavailable: 0 prevent this?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>Without a readinessProbe, Kubernetes has no signal that the new pod isn't actually ready to serve traffic yet — it may route requests to a pod that's still starting up, even though maxUnavailable: 0 correctly delayed killing the old pod.</p>
                        <table><thead><tr><th>Config</th><th>Zero dropped requests?</th></tr></thead><tbody>
