                <div class="exam-question-item"><span class="eq-number">Q3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">easypj's Backstage pods start crash-looping right after a version upgrade at 3 AM. Per the DR runbook, what's the correct first action — hotfix the running pods, or something else?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p>Confirm the blast radius first (is it Backstage or PostgreSQL?), then roll back to the last known-good image tag via ArgoCD/GitOps revert — NOT a manual hotfix. Since this follows a version bump, also re-check the upgrade helper diff.</p>
                        <table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Correct order</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                            <tr><td>Confirm blast radius</td><td>1st</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>ArgoCD/GitOps revert (not hotfix)</td><td>3rd</td></tr>
                        </tbody></table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>§26.7's DR runbook — an explicit ORDER, with "do NOT hotfix in prod" as a named instruction, not just a suggestion.</p></div>
