            <!-- ─────────── §29.1 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s29-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">29.1 Performance Optimization</h3>
                <p>Backstage performance must be tuned at every layer. Here's a systematic breakdown:</p>
                <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Bottleneck</th><th>Solution</th><th>Impact</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>Frontend</strong></td><td>Large JS bundle, slow page loads</td><td>Code splitting, lazy loading, tree shaking</td><td>🔽 40-60% load time</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Backend API</strong></td><td>Slow database queries</td><td>Query optimization, connection pooling, avoid N+1 catalog queries</td><td>🔽 50-80% query time</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Catalog Ingestion</strong></td><td>Processing 1000s of entities</td><td>Tune processing interval, limit provider scan scope</td><td>🔽 60% processing time</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Search</strong></td><td>Slow full-text queries</td><td>Reindex off-peak, cap collator batch size</td><td>🔽 70% search latency</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>TechDocs</strong></td><td>Rebuilding all docs on every change</td><td>External build storage, CDN, incremental builds</td><td>🔽 50% build time</td></tr>
                </tbody></table></div>

                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Scaling Triggers — Which Lever to Pull</div>
<pre>
  SYMPTOM                                  PULL THIS LEVER
  ----------------------------------------  --------------------------------
  High request latency, CPU maxed            Horizontal scaling (§29.2)
  Repeated identical catalog/API lookups       Caching (§29.4)
  Slow catalog processing, large entity count    Processing tuning (§29.1)
  Single point of failure, zone outage risk        High Availability (§29.3)

  Diagnose BEFORE scaling - adding replicas never fixes a caching problem,
  and caching never fixes an under-provisioned database connection pool.
</pre>
                </div>

                <p><strong>Monitoring:</strong> Track request latency, error rates, and resource usage via Prometheus/Grafana (the corrected OpenTelemetry <code>:9464/metrics</code> path from Chapter 27, not the older <code>/metrics</code> on the main port). Use Grafana dashboards to track trends and identify bottlenecks before they impact users.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ─────────── §29.2 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s29-2">
                <h3 class="section-h">29.2 Horizontal Scaling — Many Pods, One Backstage</h3>
                <div class="diagram-container"><pre class="ascii-art">
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                    LOAD BALANCER (Ingress)                   │
    │               backstage.easypj.com:443 → TLS                 │
    └───────┬──────────────────┬──────────────────┬───────────────┘
            │                  │                  │
            ▼                  ▼                  ▼
    ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐
    │ Backstage    │  │ Backstage    │  │ Backstage    │
    │ Pod 1        │  │ Pod 2        │  │ Pod 3        │
    │ (stateless)  │  │ (stateless)  │  │ (stateless)  │
    └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘
           │                 │                 │
           └─────────┬───────┴─────────┬───────┘
                     │                 │
                     ▼                 ▼
            ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐
            │ PostgreSQL   │  │ Cloud Storage │
            │ (HA Cluster) │  │ (S3/GCS/Azure)│
            │              │  │ TechDocs      │
            └──────────────┘  └──────────────┘
    </pre></div>
                <p><strong>Key points:</strong> Run 3+ replicas on K8s with HPA. Each pod is stateless — <strong>session state lives in the JWT, not pod memory</strong> — so all real state is in PostgreSQL (catalog, users) and cloud storage (TechDocs). Use <code>kubectl autoscale deployment backstage --cpu-percent=70 --min=3 --max=10</code>. Any pod can serve any request since they all connect to the same database and storage.</p>

                <div class="info-box note">
                    <h5>🔑 Advanced Lever — Service Separation</h5>
                    <p class="mb-0">Per the official scaling docs: split the backend into multiple services, each running a different set of plugins, and route requests to the right one via a custom implementation of the <code>DiscoveryService</code> interface. This is more complex than adding replicas — reach for it only after simple horizontal scaling and caching (§29.4) are already maxed out.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ─────────── §29.3 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s29-3">
