            <!-- ─────────── §29.4 ─────────── -->
            <section class="section-block" id="b-s29-4">
                <h3 class="section-h">29.4 Caching Strategies — Speed at Every Layer</h3>
                <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Cache Layer</th><th>Technology</th><th>What It Caches</th><th>TTL</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>CDN</strong></td><td>CloudFront / Cloud CDN</td><td>Static assets, TechDocs HTML</td><td>1 hour — 1 day</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Service Worker</strong></td><td>Browser SW</td><td>JS bundles, CSS, icons</td><td>Until new deploy</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Backend Cache</strong></td><td>Redis</td><td>Auth session tokens, catalog entity lookups, plugin-level response caching (e.g. GitHub API calls)</td><td>5–15 minutes</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Database</strong></td><td>PostgreSQL shared_buffers</td><td>Frequently queried entities</td><td>Automatic (LRU)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Catalog Reads</strong></td><td>In-memory (plugin)</td><td>Entity definitions</td><td>Configurable</td></tr>
                </tbody></table></div>
                <p><strong>Configuration example in app-config.yaml:</strong></p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">app-config.yaml — Cache configuration</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">backend:
  cache:
    store: redis
    connection: redis://redis.easypj.com:6379
    defaultTtl: 300  # 5 minutes in seconds
  reading:
    allow:
      - host: "backstage.easypj.com"

catalog:
  processingInterval: { minutes: 5 }  # How often to check for changes
  readCache:
    enabled: true
    maxAge: { minutes: 60 }  # Cache entity reads for 60 minutes</code></pre>
                </div>
                <p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Redis is the most impactful cache — it reduces database load by 60-80% for repeated queries. For TechDocs, a CDN in front of your cloud storage bucket provides near-instant page loads globally.</p>
            </section>

