            <section class="section-block" id="sc-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">C.1 Basic Service Template</h3>
                <p>The simplest template — scaffold any service with GitHub publishing and catalog registration. Here's the 3-step pipeline every template follows:</p>
                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Template Execution Pipeline</div><pre class="ascii-art">
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │              TEMPLATE EXECUTION PIPELINE                          │
    │                                                                  │
    │  USER CLICKS "CREATE"                                            │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ▼                                                          │
    │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
    │  │  STEP 1: fetch:template          ⏱️ ~5 seconds            │    │
    │  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │    │
    │  │  │ • Download skeleton files from template directory   │ │    │
    │  │  │ • Replace {{ parameters.name }} with actual values  │ │    │
    │  │  │ • Result: Local directory with generated code       │ │    │
    │  │  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │    │
    │  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ▼                                                          │
    │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
    │  │  STEP 2: publish:github          ⏱️ ~15 seconds           │    │
    │  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │    │
    │  │  │ • Create GitHub repository (owner/repo-name)        │ │    │
    │  │  │ • Push generated code to the new repo               │ │    │
    │  │  │ • Set up branch protection (optional)               │ │    │
    │  │  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │    │
    │  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ▼                                                          │
    │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
    │  │  STEP 3: catalog:register        ⏱️ ~3 seconds            │    │
    │  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │    │
    │  │  │ • Read catalog-info.yaml from generated repo        │ │    │
    │  │  │ • Register entity in Backstage Catalog              │ │    │
    │  │  │ • Result: Service visible in Catalog IMMEDIATELY    │ │    │
    │  │  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │    │
    │  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ▼                                                          │
    │  ✅ DONE! (~25 seconds total)                                     │
    │  Developer has: GitHub repo + CI/CD + K8s manifests + Docs       │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre></div>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">template.yaml (basic-service)</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: scaffolder.backstage.io/v1beta3
kind: Template
metadata:
  name: basic-service
  title: Basic Microservice
  description: Scaffold a new microservice from scratch
  tags: [recommended, service]
spec:
  owner: team-platform
  type: service
  parameters:
    - title: Service Details
      required: [name, owner]
      properties:
        name:
          title: Name
          type: string
          description: Unique service name
        owner:
          title: Owner
          type: string
          description: Owning team (e.g., team-platform)
        description:
          title: Description
          type: string
  steps:
    - id: fetch
      name: Fetch Skeleton
      action: fetch:template
      input:
        url: ./skeleton
    - id: publish
      name: Publish to GitHub
      action: publish:github
      input:
        repoUrl: github.com?owner=easypj&repo={{ parameters.name }}
    - id: register
      name: Register in Catalog
      action: catalog:register
      input:
        catalogInfoUrl: /catalog-info.yaml</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="card-grid cols-2">
                    <div class="info-card highlight"><div class="card-icon-lg">🔑</div><h5>3 Core Actions</h5><p>Every template uses: (1) <code>fetch:template</code> — get code, (2) <code>publish:github</code> — create repo, (3) <code>catalog:register</code> — add to catalog. Memorize this flow for the CBA.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">📝</div><h5>Parameters Drive It</h5><p>The <code>parameters</code> section defines what users fill in. Each param becomes a <code>{{ parameters.name }}</code> variable usable in steps and skeleton files.</p></div>
                </div>
            </section>

