        <article class="chapter" id="appendix-e">
            <div class="chapter-intro">
            <h2 class="chapter-title">Appendix E: Common Errors &amp; Troubleshooting</h2>
            <p class="chapter-lead">When things break (and they will), this is your first stop. Categorized by component so you can jump directly to the error you're seeing.</p>
            <div class="chapter-meta">
                <span class="meta-tag">📋 Reference</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">🔧 Troubleshooting</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">🐛 Debug</span>
            </div>
            </div><!-- /chapter-intro -->

            <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Debugging Flow — Where to Start</div><pre class="ascii-art">
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │              DEBUGGING FLOW — WHERE TO START                      │
    │                                                                  │
    │  PROBLEM: "Something's wrong with Backstage"                     │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ├── Entity not appearing? ──▶ E.1 Catalog Errors           │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ├── Template failing? ──────▶ E.2 Scaffolder Errors        │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ├── Docs not building? ─────▶ E.3 TechDocs Errors          │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ├── Can't log in? ──────────▶ E.4 Auth Errors              │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ├── Plugin not working? ────▶ E.5 Plugin Errors            │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       ├── K8s resources missing? ─▶ E.6 K8s Plugin Errors        │
    │       │                                                          │
    │       └── Backstage won't start? ─▶ E.7 Database Errors          │
    │                                                                  │
    │  💡 GENERAL TIP: Always check logs first!                        │
    │     $ kubectl logs deployment/backstage -f                       │
    │     $ yarn dev (for local — watch terminal output)               │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre></div>
            <div class="cka-exam-tip"><h5>🎯 CBA Troubleshooting Tip</h5><p class="mb-0">The CBA exam will present error scenarios and ask you to identify the root cause. The most common exam pattern: "You registered a new entity but it doesn't appear in the catalog. What's wrong?" The answer is almost always: (1) Location not configured, (2) YAML syntax error, or (3) Ingestion hasn't run yet. Always eliminate these three before looking at deeper issues.</p></div>

            <section class="section-block" id="se-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.1 Catalog Errors</h3>
                <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Error</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>Entity not found</strong></td><td>Location not configured or entity YAML has wrong <code>kind</code> or <code>name</code></td><td>Check <code>catalog.locations</code> in app-config.yaml. Verify YAML <code>kind</code> matches one of 9 valid kinds.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>YAML validation failed</strong></td><td>Indentation error, missing required field, or wrong schema</td><td>Use a YAML validator. Check <code>apiVersion</code> is <code>backstage.io/v1alpha1</code>. Verify <code>metadata.name</code> exists.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Stitching / circular dependency</strong></td><td>Two entities reference each other creating a cycle</td><td>Remove one of the circular references. Use <code>dependsOn</code> directionally (A depends on B, not both).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Location not found</strong></td><td>URL in <code>catalog.locations</code> is invalid or inaccessible</td><td>Verify the URL is reachable. Check GitHub token has read access. Try <code>curl</code> the URL directly.</td></tr>
                </tbody></table></div>
            </section>

            <section class="section-block" id="se-2">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.2 Scaffolder Errors</h3>
                <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Error</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>Template not found</strong></td><td>Wrong <code>templateRef</code> format or template name</td><td>Format: <code>template:&lt;namespace&gt;/&lt;name&gt;</code>. Check template is registered in catalog.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>publish:github failed</strong></td><td>Missing or expired GitHub token</td><td>Verify <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> env var is set. Token needs <code>repo</code> scope. Rotate if expired.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Task stuck in "processing"</strong></td><td>Action hung or timed out</td><td>Check Scaffolder logs. Restart Backstage backend. Task will timeout after 10 min (configurable).</td></tr>
                </tbody></table></div>
            </section>

            <section class="section-block" id="se-3">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.3 TechDocs Errors</h3>
                <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Error</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>Build failed</strong></td><td>Invalid <code>mkdocs.yml</code> or Markdown syntax error</td><td>Run <code>npx @techdocs/cli generate</code> locally. Check mkdocs.yml syntax. Verify Markdown is valid.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Publish failed</strong></td><td>Cloud storage permissions or credentials wrong</td><td>Verify S3/GCS bucket exists. Check IAM permissions/credentials. Test with <code>npx @techdocs/cli publish</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Docs not showing</strong></td><td>Missing <code>backstage.io/techdocs-ref</code> annotation</td><td>Add annotation to entity's catalog-info.yaml: <code>backstage.io/techdocs-ref: dir:.</code></td></tr>
                </tbody></table></div>
            </section>

            <section class="section-block" id="se-4">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.4 Auth Errors</h3>
                <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Error</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>Invalid callback / redirect_uri mismatch</strong></td><td>OAuth App callback URL doesn't match Backstage's URL</td><td>Ensure OAuth app callback matches <code>YOUR_DOMAIN/api/auth/{provider}/handler/frame</code>. Update <code>app.baseUrl</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Permission denied</strong></td><td>RBAC policy blocks the action</td><td>Check permission policies in app-config.yaml. User/group may lack required permission.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Sign-in resolver fails</strong></td><td>Identity from provider doesn't match any User entity</td><td>Create matching User entity or adjust sign-in resolver to use email/username matching.</td></tr>
                </tbody></table></div>
            </section>

            <section class="section-block" id="se-5">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.5 Plugin Errors</h3>
                <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Error</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                    <tr><td><strong>Plugin not found / 404</strong></td><td>Plugin not installed or not in <code>package.json</code></td><td>Check <code>packages/app/package.json</code>. Run <code>yarn install</code>. Verify plugin is imported in <code>App.tsx</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><strong>Plugin card shows "No data"</strong></td><td>Plugin integration credentials missing or wrong</td><td>Check plugin-specific config in app-config.yaml. Verify API tokens/env vars are set.</td></tr>
                </tbody></table></div>
            </section>

