        <article class="chapter" id="appendix-f">
            <div class="chapter-intro">
            <h2 class="chapter-title">Appendix F: Backstage Terminology Glossary</h2>
            <p class="chapter-lead">An A-Z reference for every Backstage-specific term used across this guide. If a word looks like jargon and you can't place it, it's probably here.</p>
            <div class="chapter-meta">
                <span class="meta-tag">📋 Reference</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">📖 Glossary</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">🔤 A-Z</span>
            </div>
            </div><!-- /chapter-intro -->

            <div class="comparison-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                <tr><td><strong>Annotation</strong></td><td><code>key:value</code> metadata linking an entity to an external tool</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>API (entity)</strong></td><td>Entity kind representing an API definition</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Backend</strong></td><td>Node.js/Express server layer; only layer touching the DB</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Catalog</strong></td><td>The searchable registry of ALL tracked entities</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>catalog-info.yaml</strong></td><td>The YAML file that defines one or more entities</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Component</strong></td><td>Entity kind for software YOU build</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Domain</strong></td><td>Entity kind grouping related Systems</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Entity</strong></td><td>Any "thing" tracked in the Catalog</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>EntityProvider</strong></td><td>Discovers entities automatically (ingestion)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Frontend</strong></td><td>React/MUI layer users see in the browser</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Group</strong></td><td>Entity kind for a team/squad/org unit</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Ingestion</strong></td><td>The pipeline that processes entity YAML</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Kind</strong></td><td>The TYPE of an entity (9 built-in kinds)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Label</strong></td><td><code>key:value</code> pair used to FILTER entities</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Lifecycle</strong></td><td>Entity maturity: experimental/production/deprecated</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Location</strong></td><td>A pointer to where entity YAML lives</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Metadata</strong></td><td>Common fields: name, tags, labels, annotations, links</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Owner</strong></td><td>The User/Group responsible for an entity</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Permission</strong></td><td>A named, checkable action in the permission framework</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Plugin</strong></td><td>An installable feature module (frontend/backend/full-stack)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Processor</strong></td><td>Transforms/enriches an entity AFTER discovery</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Provider</strong></td><td>Discovers WHICH entities exist (see EntityProvider)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Resource</strong></td><td>Entity kind for infrastructure you USE</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Scaffolder</strong></td><td>The template execution engine</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Sign-in resolver</strong></td><td>Maps an external identity to a Backstage User</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>spec</strong></td><td>Type-specific properties of an entity</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>System</strong></td><td>Entity kind grouping related Components + Resources</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>TechDocs</strong></td><td>Docs-as-code engine, powered by MkDocs</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Template</strong></td><td>Entity kind — a Scaffolder blueprint</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>User</strong></td><td>Entity kind for a person</td></tr>
            </tbody></table></div>

            <div class="info-box note">
                <h5>🔑 Processor vs. Provider — the pair the CBA loves to swap</h5>
                <p class="mb-0">A <strong>Provider</strong>/<strong>EntityProvider</strong> discovers WHICH entities exist in the first place (ingestion). A <strong>Processor</strong> runs AFTER that, transforming or enriching an entity that's already been discovered. See Chapter 32 §32.1 for real code showing both.</p>
            </div>
        </article>
